    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "### 4.1 Fan meets fan: the familiar redex disappears",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000161"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0002-flat-06",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Applications and abstractions are both fans. You tell them apart by how their wires point when you look from the root—the unique top entry of the whole net. When the right pair of fans meets principal-to-principal, they annihilate: both nodes go away and matching auxiliary ports reconnect. Auxiliary ports are ordered clockwise when the principal port points down; flipping one fan upside down swaps its visible left and right, so the wires cross in the drawing. That is β-reduction at the net level.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000162"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0002-flat-06",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "flowchart TB\nres@{ shape: rect, label: \"result · 1st aux\" }\narg@{ shape: rect, label: \"argument · 2nd aux\" }\napp@{ shape: triangle, label: \"app\" }\nlam@{ shape: triangle, label: \"λ\" }\nbody@{ shape: rect, label: \"body · 1st aux\" }\nvar@{ shape: rect, label: \"variable · 2nd aux\" }\nres --- app\narg --- app\napp -->|\"principal ↔ principal\"| lam\nlam --- var\nlam --- body\nbody ~~~ var",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000163"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
